  "change": "B40 plus the recorded-bias live gate (goatai#1885, agreed with Claude-Mac). In the Strategy Tester, optimization and forward, GetCurentBiasScore passes the recorded GOAT_AI_Bias_<SYM>.csv score through GOATRecordedBiasLiveScore, which rebuilds the wire state and runs the live GOATFinalizeWireV2Actionability at the run's own Bias_threshold: the score when live would act on it, otherwise -999 (below the threshold, neutral, or outside [-100,100]). A point holds until the export's own -999 row at the wire's validUntil, as live holds a record until it expires: the ~2x-row-spacing staleness heuristic does not apply to gated recorded files. A recorded point the EA treats as unavailable also pauses additions under Bias_SeqTrade, as live v2 does. The tester therefore hands the bias logic exactly what live hands it at every threshold, and the threshold stays optimisable. Tester and optimization consumption only: live paths, the input header, Astra's inputs, the trade-event policy, the bias wire and the model route are unchanged.",
